  "chem-aqa-8462-2025-p1f::10.4": "Any two from: tungsten has a much higher melting point (and boiling point) than potassium; tungsten is denser; tungsten is harder and stronger; tungsten is much less reactive (e.g. it does not react with water but potassium reacts vigorously); tungsten forms ions with different charges; tungsten forms coloured compounds; tungsten can act as a catalyst.",
